# Spine metastasis 脊椎骨轉移<div><pre class="a-b-r-La" style="user-select: text; font-family: &quot;Courier New&quot;, Courier, monospace, arial, sans-serif; line-height: normal; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: break-word; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px;">. 背架目的主要功用在於減少疼痛 (無法減少axial loading), 會讓病人試戴看看疼痛在軀幹直立狀態時是否有改善, 來決定是否需要穿背架 (因為有時病人反而覺得穿背架更不舒服).
 -&gt; Currently, there is no strong evidence about the pain control effect of brace/bed rest/mobilization.
 -&gt; However, as the patient has mechanical pain, brace is consider indicated.
 -&gt; Type of brace: Miami neck brace or 日式頸背架 (Cervical collar with thoracic extension as the lowest part of the bone mets around neck was T1).<br><pre class="a-b-r-La" style="user-select: text; font-family: &quot;Courier New&quot;, Courier, monospace, arial, sans-serif; line-height: normal; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: break-word; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px;">. Please add rivotril for possible myofascial or cervicogenic headache.</pre></pre><div></div><div><br></div></div><div><br></div><div># Lung transplant 肺移植</div><div><pre class="a-b-r-La" style="user-select: text; font-family: &quot;Courier New&quot;, Courier, monospace, arial, sans-serif; line-height: normal; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: break-word; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px;">&lt; Plan&gt; 
1. We will arrange rehabilitation programs, including bedside and home program education: 
PT evaluation.
Therapeutic Exercise, chest care, postural drainage, splinting cough, huff exercise, lung expansion exercise, diaphragm breathing, segmental breathing, spirometry, upper limbs and abdominal muscle strengthening.
2. Exercise intensity: 
   a. To tolerance if asymptomatic
   b. dyspnea rating 4-6 on a scale of 10
   c. Keep SpO2&gt; 88%, use O2 supplement if necessary
3. Stop exercise training if occurrence of the following adverse responses:
   a. Desaturation to SpO2&lt;88%
   b. Signs/symptoms of exercise intolerance: significant dyspnea or suspected acute exacerbation
